18 arms per outcome where only the median and Q1/Q3 were reported - the mean and SD are calculated from those quartiles using the Luo (2018) and Wan (2014) estimators, because no mean/SD was ever reported to begin with.
13 arms per outcome where SD was not reported but SE was - SD is back-calculated as SE x sqrt(n), the standard conversion, so a value exists to carry into the effect-size formula.



reads the documented derivation method for every effect size (c_se_derivation / ex_se_derivation) and shows how many effect sizes and studies used each method;
calculates the mean and SD only for the rows where they are genuinely missing (median/Q1/Q3 only), passes through every other reported mean and SD unchanged, and calculates the SE only where it was not already reported - then cross-checks that recalculation against the extraction team’s own *_se_analysis columns;
derives the handful of continuous fields that are still stored as free text (frequency_Hz);
checks the result against a short set of validation gates and writes the analysis-ready file that Chapter 2 reads.

7.2 Study-level rating figure
The final workbook contains 16 studies. Each tile represents the reconciled rating for one study and one adapted CRIME-Q item. Partly and Unclear are shown as separate categories because they mean different things: Partly indicates partial fulfilment of an item, whereas Unclear indicates insufficient information for a definite judgment.

crimeq_plot &lt;- ggplot(plot_dat, aes(x = Item, y = Study, fill = Rating)) +
  geom_tile(color = "#FFFDF8", linewidth = 0.65) +
  scale_fill_manual(values = rating_colors, breaks = rating_levels, drop = FALSE, name = NULL) +
  labs(x = NULL, y = NULL) +
  theme_minimal(base_size = 12) +
  theme(
    plot.background = element_rect(fill = "transparent", color = NA),
    panel.background = element_rect(fill = "transparent", color = NA),
    legend.background = element_rect(fill = "transparent", color = NA),
    legend.key = element_rect(fill = "transparent", color = NA),
    panel.grid = element_blank(),
    axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 0, hjust = 0.5, vjust = 0.5, face = "bold", color = "#242321", size = 10),
    axis.text.y = element_text(face = "bold", color = "#242321", size = 10),
    axis.ticks = element_blank(),
    legend.position = "bottom",
    legend.text = element_text(size = 11, color = "#242321"),
    legend.key.width = grid::unit(1.5, "lines"),
    plot.margin = margin(10, 10, 10, 10)
  )

crimeq_plot




Consensus CRIME-Q ratings for each included study. Green = Yes, gold = Partly, grey = Unclear, red = No, and blue = NA.





.crimeq-codebook {
  width: 100%;
  font-size: 0.93rem;
}

.crimeq-codebook th {
  background: #eef2f4;
  color: #24313a;
  vertical-align: bottom;
}

.crimeq-codebook td {
  vertical-align: top;
}

.crimeq-codebook th:first-child,
.crimeq-codebook td:first-child {
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-weight: 600;
}
